<%-
  # 2+ overloads: every section from here on is method-level, and shared
  # across every overload except when at least one overload declares its
  # own instance of a given tag family — then that family is fully
  # per-overload (each already rendered its own copy above, so there's
  # nothing left for @method's own tags to contribute) rather than a mix of
  # per-overload and shared for the same family. This section directly
  # follows the last overload's own group, with nothing else marking where
  # the per-overload group ends and the shared method-level tail begins.
  # Each heading below names its own scope explicitly (" (every overload)")
  # to disambiguate, rather than relying on a single transition marker to
  # carry that meaning for every tag type that follows it.
-%>
<%- tag_scope_suffix = overloads.size >= 2 ? " (every overload)" : "" -%>
<%- yt = overloads.size >= 2 && overloads.any? { |ov| !ov.tag(:yield).nil? } ? nil : yield_tag(@method) -%>
<%- if yt -%>
<%- yt_names = yt.types || [] -%>

**Yields<%= tag_scope_suffix %>:**

- <%= dash_join(yt_names.empty? ? "" : yt_names.map { |n| "`#{n}`" }.join(', '), yt.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- yieldparam_tags = overloads.size >= 2 && overloads.any? { |ov| !ov.tags(:yieldparam).empty? } ? [] : @method.tags(:yieldparam) -%>
<%- unless yieldparam_tags.empty? -%>

**Yield Params<%= tag_scope_suffix %>:**

<%- yieldparam_tags.each do |p| -%>
- `<%= p.name %>` (<%= type_ref_first(p) %>)<%= summary_suffix(p.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- yieldreturn_tags = overloads.size >= 2 && overloads.any? { |ov| !ov.tags(:yieldreturn).empty? } ? [] : @method.tags(:yieldreturn) -%>
<%- unless yieldreturn_tags.empty? -%>

**Yield Returns<%= tag_scope_suffix %>:**

<%- yieldreturn_tags.each do |yrt| -%>
- <%= dash_join(type_ref(yrt.types && yrt.types.join(", ")), yrt.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%-
  # 2+ overloads: no top-level Returns section when any overload declares
  # its own @return (each already rendered its own Returns above, so
  # there's nothing left for @method's own tags to contribute); otherwise
  # fall back to @method's own tags, a shared @return common to every
  # overload, rendered once here rather than duplicated per overload — the
  # same "method-level, shared" treatment @raise/@yield/@see already get.
-%>
<%- return_tags = overloads.size < 2 ? (primary ? primary.tags(:return) : method_return_tags(@method)) : (overloads.any? { |ov| !ov.tags(:return).empty? } ? [] : method_return_tags(@method)) -%>
<%- unless return_tags.empty? -%>

**Returns<%= tag_scope_suffix %>:**

<%- return_tags.each do |rt| -%>
- <%= dash_join(type_ref(rt.types && rt.types.join(", ")), rt.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- raise_tags = overloads.size >= 2 && overloads.any? { |ov| !ov.tags(:raise).empty? } ? [] : @method.tags(:raise) -%>
<%- unless raise_tags.empty? -%>

**Raises<%= tag_scope_suffix %>:**

<%- raise_tags.each do |r| -%>
- <%= dash_join(type_ref_first(r), r.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- see_tags = overloads.size >= 2 && overloads.any? { |ov| !ov.tags(:see).empty? } ? [] : @method.tags(:see) -%>
<%- unless see_tags.empty? -%>

**See also<%= tag_scope_suffix %>:**

<%- see_tags.each do |t| -%>
- <%= dash_join(see_ref(t), t.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
